title: The October Revolution
face-image: img/events/october.jpg
subtitle: The Second Congress of Soviets.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 20 and kornilov_won = 0
priority: 50
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.bol_power = RO.bolPower(Q);
Q.bol_power_d = Math.round(Q.bol_power);
Q.takeover = Q.bol_power >= 55 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.takeover) {
    Q.bol_regime = 1;
    Q.in_coalition = 0;
    Q.gov_kadets = 0;
    Q.tsereteli_advisor = 0;
    Q.skobelev_advisor = 0;
    Q.gvozdev_advisor = 0;
    Q.chkheidze_advisor = 0;
    Q.land_decree = 1;
    Q.bolshevik = 70;
    Q.repression = 2;
}
!}
go-to: oct_takeover if takeover = 1; oct_failed if takeover = 0

@oct_takeover

= The October Revolution

On the night of 7 November (25 October, Old Style) the Military Revolutionary Committee of the Petrograd Soviet, controlled by the Bolsheviks, seized the bridges, the telegraph, the railway stations and the Winter Palace. Kerensky had fled to the front. The cruiser Aurora fired a blank shell, and the cabinet was arrested.

At the Smolny Institute, the Second Congress of Soviets opened under Bolshevik control. The Menshevik and SR delegates, nearly a third of the hall, condemned the coup and walked out. Martov, who supported Lenin's right to share power but not his methods, proposed an all-socialist government, and the motion passed unanimously, and was ignored. Lenin read the Decree on Peace and the Decree on Land. The land decree is copied word for word from the SR programme.

The Bolsheviks govern in the name of the Soviets. Trotsky told the Mensheviks as they left that they had been "swept into the dustbin of history".

- @walkout: Walk out with the other moderate socialists.
- @stay: Stay in the hall and fight for a coalition.
- @lsr_join: Join the Bolsheviks at the Congress, and vote for Soviet power.

@walkout
view-if: player_party != 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 10);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, 6);
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -8, rel_ally: 2, soviet_democracy: -3});
Q.stayed_in_congress = 0;
!}

The Mensheviks and the SRs walked out and left the Congress to the Bolsheviks and the Left SRs. Martov, who was not a Bolshevik and not a Defencist, stayed long enough to propose an all-socialist government. It has never been clear whether it was a mistake to leave.

@stay
choose-if: rel_lsr >= 35 or rel_bol >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: Neither the Left SRs nor the Bolsheviks would listen.
on-arrival: {!
Q.stayed_in_congress = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 5, rel_lsr: 4, rel_ally: -3, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 10);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 14);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -4);
!}

We stayed in the hall. [? if player_party = 'menshevik' : [+ Rlbl +] and the SRs left without us; ?][? if player_party = 'sr' : The Right SRs and the Mensheviks left without us; ?]the Left SRs listened to our proposal for a coalition and half of the Bolsheviks nodded. Lenin did not. We are still in the Soviet, and still, formally, in the revolution.

@oct_failed

= The Bolsheviks Try, and Fail

On the night of 7 November the Military Revolutionary Committee called out the Red Guards and the Kronstadt sailors. The government was ready: the bridges were raised, loyal units held the Winter Palace, and Bolshevik pickets were met by Soviet militia with the support of the railwaymen. By morning, the rising had fizzled. The Bolsheviks have lost their leaders, again, and their credibility.

Lenin has once again taken refuge in Finland. Trotsky has been arrested. The Soviet parties hold the field, and the country is nobody's, yet.

What should we do about the Bolsheviks?

- @lenient: Leniency: release the arrested, and let the Bolsheviks sit in the Soviet.
- @repress: Suppress the party.

@lenient
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: -8, rel_bol: 8, soviet_democracy: 4, right_threat: -2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 6);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -4);
Q.no_terror = 1;
!}

Leniency was unpopular among [+ dlbl +], who said that it would invite another attempt. It may. But the Bolsheviks' own claim to be the champions of democracy is hard to keep up, if their leaders were pardoned by the party that they said had betrayed it.

@repress
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: -12, rel_bol: -12, right_threat: 5, repression: 6, soviet_democracy: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -2, 10);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, -4);
Q.no_terror = 0;
!}

The party was banned and its leaders imprisoned. [+ Ilbl +] said that it was the first act of a regime of terror, and the Right said that it was only a start.

@lsr_join
view-if: player_party = 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_backs_bol = 1;
Q.stayed_in_congress = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 10, rel_ally: -6, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3, workers: 2, peasants: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 4, -4);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 10);
!}

The Left SR delegates stayed in the Smolny. When Lenin read the Decree on Land, which is the SR programme almost word for word, they cheered with the Bolsheviks. Lenin has offered the party places in the government. The Left SRs have said that they will think about it, and that they would like to see a government of all the socialist parties.
